ay  based on that what's the right size of  the bag we move them around all the time  that's something that that happens  frequently for the most part consumers  seem to be very happy with it you know  we we still see volumes going up we  still can't see the number of occasions  going up so people want to want to buy  our product more and more now of course  i'm not surprised that they're engaging  in shrink-flation everyone can see that  there's less items in the bag but what i  do think is interesting is that they  also talk about sometimes they put more  chips in the bag but at the end of the  day they believe that the consumer is  happy i would love to see the metrics on  how they measure what is the consumer  happiness with how many chips are in a  bag everyone i've ever talked to they  always talk about there's too much air  and not enough chips i've never had  someone say man i love these chips  because they fill the bag all the way to  the top now shrink-flation is just  another product of what happens when you  have too much money sloshing around in  an economy but not enough supply  increasing to keep up  at the end of the day whether it's  inflation or shrink-flation the average  consumer is taking a beating  we have to get this problem under  control some of it is directly  attributed to the monetary policy some  of it is supply chain disruptions and  some of it is just the psychology in the  market as people prepare for worse  economic times  shrink flation and inflation they go  hand in hand and now we have the cfo one  of the largest companies in the world  admitting yes they do it but don't worry  the consumer loves it
 

